{"type": "assistant", "message": {"id": "msg_1785846595419", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "chatcmpl-tool-89ed0bf9be6e405e", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "python3 -c \"\nimport subprocess\nresult = subprocess.run(['pdftotext', '/tmp/streamtalk.pdf', '-'], capture_output=True, text=True)\ntext = result.stdout\n# Find conclusion/limitations\nfor kw in ['Conclusion', 'Limitation', 'limitation', 'Future', '5  ', '5.']:\n    idx = text.find(kw)\n    if idx > 0:\n        print(f'--- Found {kw} at {idx} ---')\n        print(text[idx:idx+3000])\n        break\n\" 2>&1", "description": "Find conclusion and limitations"}}], "model": "GLM-5.2-w4a8", "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "2de3dba5-b8e4-496a-a20f-317d09cd0b26", "uuid": "dfa3f86c-b05c-440a-bb19-b61f696f387e"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-89ed0bf9be6e405e", "type": "tool_result", "content": "--- Found Conclusion at 36070 ---\nConclusion\n\nWe have presented StreamTalk, a closed-loop framework for streaming co-speech\ngesture generation. By formulating clip-wise generation as sequential motion inpainting, StreamTalk introduces a retrieval-based feedback signal—Streaming\nPose-Guided Generation (SPG)—that periodically anchors each clip to the\nplausible motion manifold, transforming the conventional open-loop streaming pipeline into a closed-loop one. Stochastic Anchor Masking (SAM) bridges\nthe training–inference gap by teaching the model to inpaint complete motion\nfrom the same sparse boundary conditions that SPG provides at inference.\nA Part-aware DiT further disentangles pose from translation, enabling SPG\nto retrieve pose anchors without borrowing context-dependent global trajectories. Experiments on BEAT2 demonstrate state-of-the-art FGD under both\nsingle-speaker and multi-speaker settings, with long-horizon stability analysis\nconfirming that SPG effectively suppresses the drift accumulation inherent in\nopen-loop methods.\n\nAcknowledgments\nThis work was supported by the Alibaba Research Intern Program and the\nYoung Scientists Fund of the National Natural Science Foundation of China\nunder Grant No. 624B2110.\n\nReferences\n1. Alexanderson, S., Nagy, R., Beskow, J., Henter, G.E.: Listen, denoise, action! audiodriven motion synthesis with diffusion models. ACM Transactions on Graphics\n(TOG) 42(4), 1–20 (2023)\n2. Ao, T., Zhang, Z., Liu, L.: Gesturediffuclip: Gesture diffusion model with clip\nlatents. ACM Transactions on Graphics (TOG) 42(4), 1–18 (2023)\n3. Athanasiou, N., Petrovich, M., Black, M.J., Varol, G.: Teach: Temporal action\ncomposition for 3d humans. In: 2022 International Conference on 3D Vision (3DV).\npp. 414–423. IEEE (2022)\n4. Chen, B., Li, Y., Ding, Y.X., Shao, T., Zhou, K.: Enabling synergistic full-body\ncontrol in prompt-based co-speech motion generation. In: Proceedings of the 32nd\nACM International Conference on Multimedia. pp. 6774–6783 (2024)\n5. Chen, H., Lyu, G., Xu, C., Yan, J., Yang, X., Deng, C.: Beyond global alignment: Fine-grained motion-language retrieval via pyramidal shapley-taylor learning. arXiv preprint arXiv:2601.21904 (2026)\n6. Chen, H., Xu, C., Yan, J., Deng, C.: Astf: Motion style transfer via adaptive\nstatistics fusor. In: Proceedings of the 33rd ACM International Conference on\nMultimedia. pp. 5557–5566 (2025)\n7. Chen, J., Liu, Y., Wang, J., Zeng, A., Li, Y., Chen, Q.: Diffsheg: A diffusion-based\napproach for real-time speech-driven holistic 3d expression and gesture generation.\nIn: Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern\nRecognition. pp. 7352–7361 (2024)\n\n\f16\n\nX. Zhang et al.\n\n8. Chen, S., Wang, C., Chen, Z., Wu, Y., Liu, S., Chen, Z., Li, J., Kanda, N., Yoshioka,\nT., Xiao, X., et al.: Wavlm: Large-scale self-supervised pre-training for full stack\nspeech processing. IEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Signal Processing 16(6),\n1505–1518 (2022)\n9. Cheng, S., Zhang, J., Song, Q., Liu, S., Guo, Z., Zhang, X., Zhang", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "2de3dba5-b8e4-496a-a20f-317d09cd0b26", "uuid": "105d42e7-cfef-4be3-9ede-d26de8da9428", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T12:30:08.070Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "--- Found Conclusion at 36070 ---\nConclusion\n\nWe have presented StreamTalk, a closed-loop framework for streaming co-speech\ngesture generation. By formulating clip-wise generation as sequential motion inpainting, StreamTalk introduces a retrieval-based feedback signal—Streaming\nPose-Guided Generation (SPG)—that periodically anchors each clip to the\nplausible motion manifold, transforming the conventional open-loop streaming pipeline into a closed-loop one. Stochastic Anchor Masking (SAM) bridges\nthe training–inference gap by teaching the model to inpaint complete motion\nfrom the same sparse boundary conditions that SPG provides at inference.\nA Part-aware DiT further disentangles pose from translation, enabling SPG\nto retrieve pose anchors without borrowing context-dependent global trajectories. Experiments on BEAT2 demonstrate state-of-the-art FGD under both\nsingle-speaker and multi-speaker settings, with long-horizon stability analysis\nconfirming that SPG effectively suppresses the drift accumulation inherent in\nopen-loop methods.\n\nAcknowledgments\nThis work was supported by the Alibaba Research Intern Program and the\nYoung Scientists Fund of the National Natural Science Foundation of China\nunder Grant No. 624B2110.\n\nReferences\n1. Alexanderson, S., Nagy, R., Beskow, J., Henter, G.E.: Listen, denoise, action! audiodriven motion synthesis with diffusion models. ACM Transactions on Graphics\n(TOG) 42(4), 1–20 (2023)\n2. Ao, T., Zhang, Z., Liu, L.: Gesturediffuclip: Gesture diffusion model with clip\nlatents. ACM Transactions on Graphics (TOG) 42(4), 1–18 (2023)\n3. Athanasiou, N., Petrovich, M., Black, M.J., Varol, G.: Teach: Temporal action\ncomposition for 3d humans. In: 2022 International Conference on 3D Vision (3DV).\npp. 414–423. IEEE (2022)\n4. Chen, B., Li, Y., Ding, Y.X., Shao, T., Zhou, K.: Enabling synergistic full-body\ncontrol in prompt-based co-speech motion generation. In: Proceedings of the 32nd\nACM International Conference on Multimedia. pp. 6774–6783 (2024)\n5. Chen, H., Lyu, G., Xu, C., Yan, J., Yang, X., Deng, C.: Beyond global alignment: Fine-grained motion-language retrieval via pyramidal shapley-taylor learning. arXiv preprint arXiv:2601.21904 (2026)\n6. Chen, H., Xu, C., Yan, J., Deng, C.: Astf: Motion style transfer via adaptive\nstatistics fusor. In: Proceedings of the 33rd ACM International Conference on\nMultimedia. pp. 5557–5566 (2025)\n7. Chen, J., Liu, Y., Wang, J., Zeng, A., Li, Y., Chen, Q.: Diffsheg: A diffusion-based\napproach for real-time speech-driven holistic 3d expression and gesture generation.\nIn: Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern\nRecognition. pp. 7352–7361 (2024)\n\n\f16\n\nX. Zhang et al.\n\n8. Chen, S., Wang, C., Chen, Z., Wu, Y., Liu, S., Chen, Z., Li, J., Kanda, N., Yoshioka,\nT., Xiao, X., et al.: Wavlm: Large-scale self-supervised pre-training for full stack\nspeech processing. IEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Signal Processing 16(6),\n1505–1518 (2022)\n9. Cheng, S., Zhang, J., Song, Q., Liu, S., Guo, Z., Zhang, X., Zhang", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
